  "prompt": "Fix: the \"organize group data\" permission is not enforced on foods, tags and categories.\n\nEvery user has a can_organize flag (\"User can organize group data\") and the controllers already have a can_organize check alongside can_manage, can_invite and can_manage_household, but the tag, category and food routes never call it: any member can create, rename, delete and merge them.\n\nExpected:\n- For a user without can_organize: POST /api/organizers/tags, POST /api/organizers/categories and POST /api/foods answer 403; PUT and DELETE on /api/organizers/tags/{item_id}, /api/organizers/categories/{item_id} and /api/foods/{item_id} answer 403; PUT /api/foods/merge answers 403. A refused call changes nothing.\n- For a user with can_organize the same calls behave as today: create answers 201, update (PUT with the item's id and a new name) 200, delete 200, merge 200.\n- Reads need no permission: GET on the three collections and GET of a single item answer 200 whatever the flag.\n- The flag is read from the user at request time: granting or removing it takes effect on the next request.\n\nTests: `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/integration_tests/user_household_tests` for quick loops; the whole backend suite is `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests` (about 8 minutes).",
  "title": "fix: enforce organize-group-data permission on food/tag/category mutations (#7651)",
  "track": "fix",
